diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index a84bb01..eb0da9b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,9 +2,28 @@
 
 LakeNav WI is a personal Android lake-navigation prototype focused on Wisconsin inland lakes and Great Lakes use.
 
-## Version 0.5 features
+## Version 0.6 features
 
-Version 0.5 keeps the v0.4 navigation, bathymetry, hazard, offline-lake, waypoint, GPS tracking, weather, and DNR features while focusing on a more current 2026-style interface and calmer heading behavior.
+Version 0.6 builds on the v0.5 interface and heading improvements with a selectable Auto / GPS Course / Compass heading source, a quick map-layer popover, and an animated wind field overlay for rapid weather awareness.
+
+
+### Quick map layers
+- Adds a floating Layers control directly on the map.
+- Quickly toggles NOAA chart display, NOAA depth colors, hazards/nav aids, and animated wind without opening the full Lake Tools sheet.
+- Keeps the existing full settings available for longer-form controls.
+
+### Heading source selector
+- Adds **Auto**, **GPS**, and **Compass** modes.
+- Auto is recommended: it prefers GPS course-over-ground once movement and bearing accuracy are good enough, otherwise it uses the phone true-heading compass.
+- GPS mode intentionally waits for adequate movement instead of treating a stationary GPS bearing as real heading.
+- Compass mode forces the phone true-heading compass for stationary testing and calibration.
+
+### Animated wind overlay
+- Samples modeled current 10-meter wind across the visible map and animates particles in the wind-flow direction.
+- Uses Open-Meteo data in the personal/non-commercial test build and shows a current modeled wind speed/direction summary.
+- Refreshes when the map is moved far enough or after the cached wind field ages.
+- Requires data service and is disabled in LakeNav Offline mode.
+- This is forecast/model guidance, not a replacement for local observations or an onboard anemometer.
 
 ### 2026 interface refresh
 - Reworks the top status area, map chips, compass, bottom navigation dock, cards, buttons, search controls, and bottom sheets with a cleaner modern visual system.
